                "ImageDescription": {
                  "value": "A carte-de-visite of a young Harriet Tubman seated in an interior room. Photographed by Benjamin F. Powelson in 1868-69. \nOriginally owned by <a class=\"external text\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Emily%20Howland\">Emily Howland</a>, an abolitionist Quaker schoolteacher who lived in <a class=\"external text\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sherwood,_New_York\">Sherwood NY</a>, just a few miles from where Tubman lived in <a class=\"external text\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Auburn,_New_York\">Auburn, NY</a>, the town where the image was taken. Jointly purchased by the National Museum of African American History and Culture  and the Library of Congress in 2017.",
